Binary archive header: match ZenGin's layout (no date/user, 9-char object count).

WriteArchiveBinary::write_header stamped `date ` and `user ` lines and padded the
object count to a 10 character field. ZenGin's zCArchiverBinary never writes
either line and uses a 9 character field: every retail Gothic II world (NewWorld,
OldWorld, AddonWorld nested MATLIST archives) and every compiled .MSH file under
_work/Data/Meshes reads `...saveGame 0\nEND\nobjects 1400     \nEND\n\n`. The
header is now written that way, which also removes this writer's use of the
glibc-only strftime("%-d...") format.

